WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.340
Hey youtubers, it’s Charlie and the Oscars
are here.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.779
I’ll be doing a proper Oscars Winner video
later tonight, but before that I wanted to

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:13.180
do a video for all the fandoms and fandom
actors that we wish would win an Oscar.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:18.640
Because the Oscars are the most professionally
respected awards I’m bending rules and including

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.319
things like Doctor Who and television shows
based on certain criteria.

00:00:21.319 --> 00:00:25.929
Oscars are for motion pictures only and you
could argue that the People’s Choice Awards

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:28.060
is kind of like the Fandom Oscars.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.550
But the real Oscars are voted on by a group
of Hollywood peers.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.550
Mostly old men.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:37.330
So let’s just have some fun with this and
do best picture, best actor, best actress

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.340
and best supporting actor and actress.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.750
The really funny thing about all this is that
sometimes actors that win real life Oscars

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.490
actually have starred in some of your favorite
fandoms in the past.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:50.510
It’s just that some people or directors
or writers get there start on a science fiction

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.990
or genre show and then later in life go on
to become hugely successful.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:58.310
But part of the reason I wanted to do this
is that most of the time the people that Vote

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.960
on the real life Oscars really hate Science
Fiction and genre.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.119
For instance Christopher Nolan has only ever
been nominated for an Oscar for his Memento

00:01:06.119 --> 00:01:08.770
screenplay and for Inception.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:09.799
He didn’t win either.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:14.880
Inception lost to King’s Speech, which is
exactly the kind of movie you call Oscar-Bait.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.650
So let’s talk about our favorite Fandoms
we think deserve Oscars.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.370
Remember for this two-part episodes count
as a movie.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:25.110
Let’s start with Best Supporting Actress
- We have to start with Michelle Fairly for

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.110
The Red Wedding.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.859
She’s amazing as Catelyn Stark in general
and since the show is so serialized I’ll

00:01:30.859 --> 00:01:31.930
include her.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:39.210
Then there’s Amanda Abbington in His Last
Vow as Mary Morstan, now Mary Morstan Watson.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.530
They have to compete with Evangeline Lily,
one of the few females in Desolation of Smaug

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.659
this year, but an amazing performance nonetheless.

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:50.789
Feel free to make any additions for supporting
actresses in your favorite fandom in the comments.

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:52.399
Next is best supporting actor.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:55.939
We have to include Lars Mikkelsen as Charles
Augustus Magnussen.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:57.130
Such a great villain.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.560
And every bit as scary as his brother Mads
Mikkelsen in Hannibal.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.020
Then there’s both David Tennant and John
Hurt in the Doctor Who 50th Anniversary.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:11.830
Then there’s Philip Seymour Hoffman in Catching
Fire, Idris Elba in Pacific Rim and I’d

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:16.330
like to nominate all of the dwarves from Desolation
of Smaug as one collective group.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.980
They could just share one Oscar statue if
they won.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.760
Technically I consider Richard Armitage to
be one of the main star’s so I’ll nominate

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.020
him when I get to Best Actor.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.460
Technically we also need to include Benedict
Cumberbatch.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.770
I consider Smawg to be a supporting character
even though he’s so big.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.600
Now it’s time for Best Actress though.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.500
These are the leads from each movie or fandom.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.790
Starting off with the easy one.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.360
Jennifer Lawrence in Catching Fire.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.680
She’ll get attention at the actual Oscars
for American Hustle, but it’s probably her

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.320
Hunger Games stuff that most of us know her
from.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.960
The other easy ones being Sandra Bullock in
Gravity.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.090
And Scarlett Johansson in Her.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.460
Great science fiction if you haven’t seen
them yet.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.870
Some of the few science fiction movies that
are actually getting legit recognition this

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.870
awards season.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.761
There’s actually a lot of actresses on my
list in genre movies for this so I’ll try

00:02:56.761 --> 00:02:58.431
to cut it down to the best.

00:02:58.431 --> 00:03:00.650
Jessica Chastain in Guillermo Del Toro’s
Mama.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.900
It’s a horror movie.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.490
Rinko Kikuchi in Pacific Rim, one of the most
badass female characters all year.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.080
Both Kristin Bell and Idina Menzel in Frozen.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.600
They should all win for Let It Snow too.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.980
And I can’t leave off Amy Acker in Joss
Whedon’s Much Ado About Nothing.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.630
On to best Actor.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.600
Starting off with Benedict Cumberbatch and
Martin Freeman for the entirety of Sherlock

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:29.250
Series 3, Matt Smith in the 50th Anniversary
Special, Tony Leung in Won Kar-Wai’s Grandmaster

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.730
as Ip Man, so awesome.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.300
Alexis Denisof also in Much Ado About Nothing.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.260
I kind of want to include Tom Hiddleston for
Only Lovers Left Alive, but they moved the

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.490
release date so technically it’s a 2014
movie.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.490
And lastly Peter Dinklage, in everything.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.130
But mostly Game of Thrones this season.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.770
So here’s my best picture pics.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.710
I tried to narrow it down to the best of the
best.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.680
There were a lot of awesome things, and some
of them are actually getting recognized at

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.010
the real life Oscars.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:01.870
But first there’s Spike Jonze’s Her, it
was actually my favorite theatrical film next

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.310
to Miyazaki’s The Wind Rises.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.400
Those are two movies you have to see.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.870
Wind Rises is actually nominated for best
Foreign Language film, which I hope it wins.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.210
But I think it should be included for Best
Picture overall.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:18.010
Then there’s Desolation of Smaug, it was
one of the only movies in addition to The

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.560
Wind Rises that I paid to see more than once
in a movie theater.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:26.250
Then Gravity from Alfonso Cuaron, I love all
of his movies, but Gravity is amazing.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.500
And that’s my list, let me know what your
favorite sci fi or genre movie was this year

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.130
and whether or not you think it deserves an
Oscar.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.250
Like I said, I’ll be doing a real Oscar
Winner’s video tonight.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.470
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.990
I’ll also be posting a new Walking Dead
Episode.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.780
Right now click here for that Oscar Winners
Video.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.000
I’ll add the annotation tonight when I post
it.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.000
And Click here to catch up on Walking Dead
before tonight’s episode.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.120
Thanks for watching, see you tonight.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:51.820
High Fives!

